      "writtenOn": "2025-08-12T20:03:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "CMA memory is not marked reserved to start with, indeed it\u0027s part of the system memory. GCMA is a reserved memory, therefore once system wants to use it we should mark it unreserved. We can do that during GCMA init but I think that would be semantically incorrect. If we don\u0027t do that here then when we free the free_pages_prepare() will trigger a bad page report.",
